{%- comment -%}
  The Instagram strip — one row of square crops, scrolling. Port of
  components/home/instagram-strip.tsx.

  The track holds the run twice and travels exactly -50%, so the loop is seamless
  (.wl-marquee in base.css). It runs continuously — hovering does not stop it —
  and prefers-reduced-motion stops it altogether, which is why the rail is
  overflow-x-auto rather than hidden: with the animation off, the strip has to
  stay reachable by scrolling. The scrollbar chrome is taken off by .wl-rail, so
  that fallback costs the design nothing.

  This section costs no JavaScript. Keep it that way, and do NOT wrap it in
  anything that animates opacity.

  The images are the catalogue's own, since the studio's posts are not wired up.
  There are no links on them for the same reason — a post needs a permalink, and
  inventing one would send readers nowhere.

  DEVIATION — the heading is a label, not a section head. The design gave it the
  same centred H2 treatment as New arrivals and the voices wall, which billed it
  as a peer section; it has no links and no studio posts, only the catalogue's
  own photographs. It is now --text-label uppercase, which states what the strip
  is without claiming to be a destination. The element and its id stay put:
  aria-labelledby="instagram-heading" is the section's accessible name.
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- liquid
  assign source = collections[section.settings.collection]
  assign shown = section.settings.count
-%}

<section aria-labelledby="instagram-heading" class="flex flex-col gap-7 py-section">
  <h2 id="instagram-heading" class="px-gutter text-center font-body text-label uppercase tracking-nav text-ink-subtle">
    {% render 'copy', value: section.settings.heading, label: 'heading' %}
  </h2>

  <div class="wl-marquee wl-rail overflow-x-auto [mask-image:linear-gradient(90deg,transparent,#000_5%,#000_95%,transparent)]">
    <ul class="wl-marquee-track">
      {%- comment -%} Two runs, so translateX(-50%) lands exactly where it started. {%- endcomment -%}
      {%- comment -%}
        A partially stocked collection is a THIRD fact, and neither branch used to
        handle it. The old shape was "any products at all -> render them, otherwise
        render `shown` placeholders", so a collection holding one piece drew exactly
        one tile and the rest of the rail was empty. On the marquee that also killed
        the motion: a two-tile track is narrower than the viewport, so translateX(-50%)
        had nothing to travel over and the strip sat still looking broken. It will
        happen again on the real import, which lands eleven pieces one at a time.
        So: render what exists, then top up with labelled placeholders to `shown`.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      {%- for copy in (0..1) -%}
        {%- assign real = source.products.size -%}
        {%- if real > shown -%}{%- assign real = shown -%}{%- endif -%}
        {%- assign pad = shown | minus: real -%}
        {%- for product in source.products limit: shown -%}
          <li class="w-58 shrink-0" {% if copy == 1 %}aria-hidden="true"{% endif %}>
            {% render 'media', image: product.featured_image, sizes: '232px', ratio: '1 / 1', label: 'Studio post', class: 'rounded-none' %}
          </li>
        {%- endfor -%}
        {%- if pad > 0 -%}
          {%- for i in (1..pad) -%}
            <li class="w-58 shrink-0" {% if copy == 1 %}aria-hidden="true"{% endif %}>
              {% render 'media', image: nil, sizes: '232px', ratio: '1 / 1', label: 'Studio post', class: 'rounded-none' %}
            </li>
          {%- endfor -%}
        {%- endif -%}
      {%- endfor -%}
    </ul>
  </div>
</section>

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "Instagram strip",
  "settings": [
    { "type": "collection", "id": "collection", "label": "Photograph source" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "heading", "label": "Heading", "default": "Follow us on Instagram" },
    { "type": "range", "id": "count", "label": "Photographs", "min": 6, "max": 16, "step": 1, "default": 11 }
  ],
  "presets": [{ "name": "Instagram strip" }]
}
{% endschema %}
